WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.170
- [Kelly] Let's close the show out

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.820
with something positive from the internet.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.863
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:03.863 --> 00:00:06.630
(energetic music)

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.130
- Most high school seniors

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.840
are a few months from graduation

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.190
but in Pennsylvania,

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.620
a nine year old has them all beat.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.520
This is David,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.180
who just received his
high school diploma. What?

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.060
The aspiring astrophysicist
took online classes

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.155
during the pandemic and
graduated with a 4.27 GPA.

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:26.850
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.250
He's also in Mensa. Sure.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.050
Let's get this amazing kid in here,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.630
everybody say hello to
David and his mama, Ronya,

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.530
watching on WGALA.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.350
What's up y'all?

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.183
How ya doing?

00:00:39.144 --> 00:00:40.980
- We're doing well, how are you?

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.750
- You're doing better than well, ma'am.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.610
Y'all are killing it in your household.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.760
So David, congratulations
on finishing high school.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.960
Is it true that you didn't think

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.210
this was like a big deal?

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.580
- Yeah, me and my mom had a back and forth

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.437
and I'm like, okay, I
graduated. That's very nice.

00:00:56.437 --> 00:00:59.730
"You graduated at the age of
nine. This is incredible."

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.060
And so I finished elementary
school in half a year,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.550
I finished middle school in one year,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.740
and then I finished
high school in one year.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.170
And so she, and so she has to explain

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:15.170
to me about how, okay, you
graduated at the age of nine,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.080
look at how you finished the
grades like in two months.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.170
- I'm just telling you right
now, you are exceptional.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.360
That is not a, normally

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.000
I mean I have a six and
eight year old, David.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.070
They're not on the same
path is all I'm saying,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.000
Like most aren't.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.920
And Ronya, this is, this is

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.440
something you felt you had to do. Why?

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.540
- I needed to challenge my son.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.280
He's a gift from God and I felt

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.410
that I have to give him
the best that I got.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.820
So I had to do a lot of research.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.950
I had to look into things, I had to learn

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.570
I had to get outside of the box

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:49.260
to challenge my child the way he deserves.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.180
- Do you, did you, okay 'cause look,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.860
I do homework with
like, my kids sometimes.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.660
And I, I, and I used to have
other kids in my household too,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.130
and so there would be older homework

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.800
and I'd be like Google

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.320
'cause I forgot, like
were you ever doing work

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.650
with him and going, I
don't know. Like, (laughs)

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.013
- Yes, there have been times,
- Oh my gosh, I love-

00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:09.420
- that's happened, I
had to go to his father

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.550
'cause he's the guru, in certain things.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.980
We split the subjects.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.260
He has certain subjects that he's good at

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.700
like English and Finances.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.620
I have Math and Science.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.030
- Oh my god, you're like my sister.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.380
She's the same way with
that kind of stuff.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.910
I love that David was gonna out you,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.743
he was like, yeah, no,

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:27.240
she got lost a few times like,

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.520
but thank you so much
David and thank you Ronya,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.750
exceptional family y'all,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.155
I'm liking your post right now, right.

00:02:32.155 --> 00:02:33.603
(bell chimes)

00:02:33.603 --> 00:02:35.490
- [Ronya] Thank you.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.480
- And that's not all,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.280
our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.020
makers of Frixion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.070
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.840
want to celebrate people going

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.550
after big dreams just like you.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.290
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars,

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.140
how's that sound?

00:02:48.622 --> 00:02:50.613
- Wow. Amazing. Thank you very much.

00:02:51.497 --> 00:02:54.127
- Aw, like look at his face! (laughing)

00:02:54.127 --> 00:02:55.410
Good luck David,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.940
you're gonna kill it in life!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.920
You're already doin' it!

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.540
Thank you to all our guests this hour:

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.490
Jane Lynch, Bozoma Saint John,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.600
Kevin Jonas, and Rachel.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.433
Y'all have a great day

00:03:04.433 --> 00:03:06.130
and if it's not, try and change it.

